experiment: ippool
  instrument        ippool   trial seed 0000000001353e69   4857 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          stageprobe put the compression in intrinsic plasticity
                    (bias->rate 0.34 on, 0.91 off). DNA v57 pools the rate
                    error per articulator group: regulation holds and the
                    transfer recovers to 0.51. Does that buy delivered dF1?
  the gate          EXCESS over each arm's OWN matched-marginal control,
                    ip9 vs ip0, PAIRED on seed, at 2 SE -- and the ip9 mean
                    rate must stay regulated, or it is v50's refuted trade.
  stated up front   n = 18, and a 2-3 SE result at that size is a HYPOTHESIS
                    in this project; three have been retracted. And a null
                    here does not rule out a convergence-SPEED effect.


  ARM LIVENESS vs `ip0` (seeds where the arm differs at all)
    ip0-rnd            18/18
    ip9                18/18
    ip9-rnd            18/18

  arm       dF1 (Hz)         aligned     gain      larynx rate
  ip0        103.9 +/- 8.8     0.04581     3.09      4.62
  ip0-rnd     28.0 +/- 4.4     0.01475     0.87      4.74
  ip9         87.5 +/- 13.8    0.02373     1.71      5.50
  ip9-rnd     27.2 +/- 5.3     0.01393     0.84      5.30

  EXCESS DIFFERENCE, ip9 - ip0, paired on seed
    -15.6 +/- 17.5  (-0.90 SE)   signs 8/18
  larynx rate  ip0 4.62 Hz, ip9 5.50 Hz, drift 19%

  RELIEVING THE BOTTLENECK DOES NOT BUY dF1. The transfer improves
  0.34 -> 0.51 and the delivered formant does not follow at 2 SE. So the
  compression is necessary for the ceiling but not sufficient to lift it:
  half the relief buys nothing measurable, and the honest reading is that
  the remaining 0.51 -> 0.91 is where any gain would be -- which needs no
  rate regulation at all, and v50 priced that at +16.6 -> -2.3.
